course: dictionary
lesson: 4140
title: Gloomy: dark, sad or bad news
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gloomy has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. It can mean dark or dim with very little light, like «a gloomy castle». It can mean sad and without hope, like «feel gloomy». It can also mean expecting bad things, like «a gloomy forecast».
explain: «The passage is long, gloomy, and, to tell the truth, decidedly shabby.» The clues are long and shabby, so gloomy means dark and dim. Check by swapping in your meaning: a dark and dim passage still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: «The Rat whispers that Badger is always gloomy when he is hungry.» This is about a mood, not a place. Badger is low and sad when he is hungry. Eeyore is gloomy in the same way, and that is how we know he is unhappy.
fact: Gloomy is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a gloomy day, a gloomy face. Its forms are gloomy, gloomier and gloomiest.
fact: Gloomy can mean dark or dim with very little light, as in «a gloomy castle».
fact: Gloomy can mean sad and without hope, as in «feel gloomy» or «a gloomy face».
fact: Gloomy can mean expecting bad things to happen, as in «gloomy news» or «a gloomy forecast».
fact: In weather talk, «dreich» in Scotland means grey, damp and gloomy, and «chucking it down» in the UK means raining hard.
exercise: «The cellar was gloomy, with only one dim lamp.» What does gloomy mean here? | Loud and full of music | Happy and full of laughter | *Dark and dim, with very little light | Hot and sunny
exercise: «The forecast is gloomy, so expect rain all week.» What does gloomy mean in this forecast? | Full of bright stars | Very cheerful | Lost in the mist | *Expecting bad things to happen
exercise: «Eeyore is gloomy and sad, and he sighs all day.» Which word tells you Eeyore's mood is low? | sighs | all day | Eeyore | *gloomy
test: «He felt gloomy after losing the match.» What does gloomy mean? | Very hungry | Full of bright colour | Quick and clever | *Sad and without hope
test: «The Rat whispers that Badger is always gloomy when he is hungry.» What is Badger's mood when he is hungry? | Excited and full of energy | Sleepy and calm | *Low and sad | Brave and bold
exam: Which sentence uses gloomy to mean expecting bad things? | «She loved her new bike and rode it to school.» | «The sun was bright and warm all day.» | *«The gloomy forecast says the storm will come tomorrow.» | «The cat slept by the fire.»
